  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**  \n   **Central Idea:** We employ a **hierarchical variational approach** with two levels:  \n   - **Upper Bound Relaxation:** Formulate the problem as a **convex optimization problem** softened with exponential cones to approximate the maximum overlap.  \n   - **Lower Bound Realization:** Solve the relaxed problem using sparse solutions and lift them to the original space with a **greedy refinement strategy**.  \n   This combines the efficiency of convex optimization with the flexibility of sparse representations to escape local optima.  \n\n   **Key Bottlenecks Addressed:**  \n   - **Non-convexity:** Directly solving the original problem is intractable. Use relaxation to create a tractable proxy.  \n   - **Lack of Structure:** Ensure the solution respects period doubling and spectral decay through frequency constraints.  \n   - **Tractability:** Optimize in log-domain to separate scale and phase, making the objective smooth and convex-friendly.  \n\n   **Limitations:**  \n   - The relaxation is an upper bound: solutions found are valid bounds but not necessarily the optimum.  \n   - Requires careful initialization to avoid trapped eigenvectors.  \n   - While sparse, the solution must later be refined to ensure boundedness and integral constraints.  \n\n   **Guidance:**  \n   This approach is a **structural change** from the previous grid-based optimization. We use logarithmic transforms and exponential cones directly, unlike the grid-specific penalties. The method prioritizes discovery over refinement, making it different from the fine-grained L-BFGS and active-set local searches.  \n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**  \n   **Representation:**  \n   Represent the step function via its **logarithmic derivative** to decouple scale and phase:  \n   \\[\n   h(x) = \\sigma(w(x)), \\quad w(x) = \\sum_{k} c_k \\phi_k(x)\n   \\]  \n   where \\(\\phi_k(x)\\) are periodic basis functions (Fourier modes) and \\(c_k\\) are coefficients.  \n\n   **Constraints:**  \n   - **Integral Constraint:** \\(\\int_0^2 h(x)  dx = 1\\)  \n   - **Boundedness:** \\(0 \\leq h(x) \\leq 1\\)  \n   - **Frequency Decay:** Enforce constraints on the decay of Fourier coefficients for stability.  \n\n   **Objective:**  \n   The minimum overlap is bounded via:  \n   \\[\n   \\min_{h} \\max_k \\int h(x)(1-h(x+k))  dx\n   \\]  \n   Replaced with a **smoothed exponential penalty** in the log-domain:  \n   \\[\n   \\text{Object}(w) = \\max_k \\min_{c,\\phi} \\left( \\|w(x) - \\log(c) \\| + \\lambda \\sum_k |w_k|\\right) \n   \\]  \n   **Derivations:**  \n   - Use **Wirtinger derivatives** in Sobolev spaces.  \n   - Equation-based solver with spectral initialization.  \n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**  \n   **Phases:**  \n   `a) Initialization`  \n   - Start with a **periodic Gaussian beam** or **Fourier-basis projection**.  \n   - Ensure periodicity via circulant matrices.  \n   **b) Hierarchical Optimization**  \n   - **Log-Domain Relaxation:** Transform to log-space to expose smooth convexity.  \n   - **Exponential Cone Programming:** Solve the auxiliary problem using ECOS or MOSEK.  \n   - **Projection:** Map back to real space with soft thresholding.  \n   **c) Adaptive Resolution**  \n   - Start with \\(n\\text{base}=50\\) samples.  \n   - Double the resolution every \\(80\\) seconds (up to \\(n=400\\)).  \n   - Use **progressive basis expansion** for higher phases.  \n\n4. **Search Choices**  \n   **a) Basis Functions:**  \n   - Use Fourier basis (\\(\\sin(2\\pi n x / L), \\cos(2\\pi n x / L)\\)) with \\(L=2\\).  \n   - Add wavelet bases for better approximation near discontinuities.  \n   **b) Hyperparameters:**  \n   - \\(\\lambda = 1.2 \\times (\\text{frequency}^{-1} )\\) for stabilization.  \n   - Initialize with \\(spectrum \\cdot exp(-\\alpha |k|)\\) for decay.  \n   **c) Optimization Strategy:**  \n   - **Stall Detection:** Switch to an **evolution strategy** if function decreases stall.  \n   - **Intervention Schedule:** Double resolution every 300 function evaluations.  \n\n5. **Compute Budget**  \n   - **Phase 1 (Log-transform & Initialization):** 10% budget.  \n   - **Phase 2 (Exponential Cone):** 60% budget.  \n   - **Phase 3 (Resolution Doubling):** 30% budget.  \n   - Check progress every minute to adjust \\(\\alpha\\) for basis decay.  \n\n6. **Validation and Contract**  \n   **Feasibility Checks:**  \n   - Integral: \\(\\sum \\text{samples} \\cdot dx \\equiv 1\\) (adjust via constraint projections).  \n   - Boundedness: Clip coefficients beyond valid range (e\u207b\u2078 to e\u00b9).  \n   **Acceptance:**  \n   - Compute exact \\(C_5\\) only at final \\(n=400\\) grid.  \n   - Fallback: Use nearest neighbor projection if relaxed solution fails.  \n   **Graceful Degradation:**  \n   - If evaluation stalls, switch to random restarts.  \n   - Reduce \\(\\lambda\\) on stall to avoid drowning.  \n**Final Implementation Notes:** Direct equivalent of the approach will be written by a separate agent, leveraging CVXPY with exponential cone support. The code will strictly enforce the hierarchical structure described here.",
